PRE-EXISTING (not introduced by batch4) — spurious store_auto_opened on the directStore boot tier.

WHERE: UserApp splash directStore boot when there is NO persisted address but the saved-address book
       has the zone-3 default (the NEARS-469 "auto-select most-recent saved address" path — i.e. the
       first cold boot after login). Home mounts on this path ("home load started" x2) and
       SingleStoreHeroView can build and fire its impression event even though the user is navigated
       straight into store 59 and never sees the hero.

SYMPTOM: store_auto_opened (the HERO IMPRESSION event) fires on a boot where the hero was never shown,
         alongside store_direct_opened. This is exactly the distinction destination_resolver.dart:248-250
         declares load-bearing ("§6.2 - distinct boot-entry event (keeps `store_auto_opened` hero
         impression semantics intact)") and that the nav guide records as
         "Confirm via store_direct_opened (NOT store_auto_opened)". It inflates the hero-impression metric.

OBSERVED (emulator-5554):
  analytics: sectors_shown       {sectors_count: 1, zone_id: 3}
  analytics: store_direct_opened {store_id: 59, module_id: 4, zone_id: 3}
  analytics: store_auto_opened   {store_id: 59, module_id: 4, zone_id: 3}   <-- spurious
  analytics: view_store          {store_id: 59}

IT IS A RACE, AND IT PRE-DATES THIS BATCH — like-for-like, same boot path, same device:
  pre-fix baseline (ebeddafe, i.e. WITHOUT NEARS-1051/1052):  store_auto_opened in 2 of 4 cold boots
  batch4          (4dea472d):                                 store_auto_opened in 3 of 4 cold boots
  (persisted-address directStore boot: CLEAN on both builds — 0/1 baseline, 0/2 batch4)
Both builds show "home load started" x2 on this path, so the underlying cause (Home mounting during a
directStore boot) is present in both. The rate difference is within noise at n=4 and no ordering change
in d3617074 accounts for it (the disarm and the terminal nav both sit inside _navigateOnce, which
completes before Home is navigated to).

=> Filed as a PRE-EXISTING defect, not a batch4 regression. Does not gate this ticket.
